::: {.cell}

Amyloidosis is characterized by extracellular deposition of misfolded protein fibrils causing progressive organ dysfunction. Diagnosis relies on Congo Red staining with apple-green birefringence under polarized light. Subtypes are classified by immunohistochemical staining for light chain, AA, or transthyretin protein.
